  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved the best result so far (acc 0.678, F1 0.646), a modest +2.8 pp gain over the best RNA-only config (config_005, acc 0.650). The image modality alone was very weak (0.208), so the source of the multimodal gain is uncertain. Question: Does the fusion mechanism (weighted vs. concat) materially affect performance in this best-performing multimodal setup? config_030 is identical to config_031 except it uses concat fusion, providing a clean one-variable A/B test. Why this is the best use of the next budget slot: it is the lowest-uncertainty, highest-information experiment available—it directly clarifies whether the learned weighted fusion is a meaningful design choice or whether any fusion strategy yields similar results. This knowledge determines whether subsequent multimodal experiments should prioritize weighted fusion, and it avoids over-investing in a fusion mechanism whose contribution is currently confounded with the overall multimodal gain."
}

